            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. A shopkeeper serves you cold lassi in a tumbler. By chance, the tumbler had a small leak. You were given another tumbler by the shopkeeper to put the leaky tumbler in it. Will this arrangement help to keep the lassi cold for a longer time? Explain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.348,
            0.742,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. State with reason(s) whether the following statements are True [T] or False [F]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.391,
            0.614,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Heat transfer takes place in solids through convection. [ ]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.429,
            0.742,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Heat transfer through convection takes place by the actual movement of particles. [ ]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.467,
            0.743,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Areas with clay materials allow more seepage of water than those with sandy materials. [ ]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.505,
            0.742,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) The movement of cooler air from land to sea is called land breeze. [ ]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.543,
            0.743,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Some ice cubes placed in a dish melt into water after sometime. Where do the ice cubes get heat for this transformation?"
